    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="5c3b06de-9135-5505-a1b5-e731a2d648fa" activityNameId="22763c3e-5096-560d-b4f0-a3e4415d5f61" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Inert material landfill facility</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Inert material landfill facility
landfill for inert, insoluble, largely unpolluted, mostly mineral wastes like bricks, concrete, excavation material with carbon content below 5%. 450'000 m3 volume. Construction phase is 1 year;
Synonyms: cleanfill; 
UUID: 080e3d3b-2a77-3164-93f9-6c3d5d229743
infrastructure materials for landfill construction, operation and aftercare. Including access road.
Location: Specific to the technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Well applicable to modern landfilling practices in Europe, North America or Japan.
Technology: Swiss iner material landfill ("cleanfill") for largely unpolluted, inorganic wastes. 50% of the sites feature a base seal and leachate collection system. Recultivation and monitoring for 5 years after closure.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: data from one literature source on sanitary landfill, adapted to features of this landfill type 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_080e3d3b-2a77-3164-93f9-6c3d5d229743.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">CH</shortname>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Location: Specific to the technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Well applicable to modern landfilling practices in Europe, North America or Japan.</text>
